course: dictionary
lesson: 13160
title: Formulate: thinking it out and putting it into words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To formulate something means to think it out carefully and put it together in detail. «Before we start, we must formulate a plan for the science project.» The plan is not finished until it is worked out step by step.
explain: You can also formulate by saying something clearly in words or symbols. «Can you formulate your question so the whole class understands it?» The question must be clear, not rushed or messy.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Plan, idea, question, rule and hypothesis all point to careful thinking. Try the swap test: put "think out carefully" into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: «Formulate» means to think something out carefully and put it together in detail.
fact: «Formulate a hypothesis» means to make a clear prediction before you test it in an experiment.
fact: Companies formulate new products, such as shampoos, by deciding which ingredients to mix together and how much of each to use.
fact: The forms are formulate (now), formulates (he or she), formulated (before now) and formulating (happening now): «She formulated her idea yesterday.»
exercise: «Before the experiment, Sam formulated a hypothesis.» What does formulated mean here? | Forgot all about | *Thought out carefully and put into words | Threw away | Broke into pieces
exercise: «The chef formulated a new shampoo from natural oils.» What does formulated mean in this sentence? | To wash the dishes quickly | To lose something important | To shout loudly at the team | *To make something from a particular mixture
exercise: «The team formulated a plan to win the match.» Which word tells you what was formulated? | team | *plan | match | formulated
test: «Mia needed to formulate a question for her science project.» What does formulate mean here? | Run quickly to the lab | Colour in the picture | Forget about it completely | *Think out carefully and put into clear words
test: Which is the best meaning of «formulate a hypothesis»? | Copy it from a friend | Ignore the experiment | Throw the results away | *Make a clear prediction to test later
exam: Pupil asks, «What does it mean to formulate a rule?» Which answer is best? | To break the rule on purpose | To write it in pencil only | *To think it out carefully and put it into clear words | To make up a silly game
